From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] audio-settings: honour allow-volume-above-100-percent

PhoshAudioSettings has an allow_volume_above_100_percent field that is
checked but never set, so the volume slider stopped at 100% even with
org.gnome.desktop.sound allow-volume-above-100-percent true (phosh
0.56.0).  Read the key when the widget is built.
---
--- a/src/settings/audio-settings.c
+++ b/src/settings/audio-settings.c
@@ -361,6 +361,15 @@
 
   gtk_widget_init_template (GTK_WIDGET (self));
 
+  /* allow_volume_above_100_percent was never set, so the slider stopped at
+   * 100% whatever org.gnome.desktop.sound said.  Read it once. */
+  {
+    g_autoptr (GSettings) sound = g_settings_new ("org.gnome.desktop.sound");
+
+    self->allow_volume_above_100_percent =
+      g_settings_get_boolean (sound, "allow-volume-above-100-percent");
+  }
+
   mixer_control = phosh_audio_manager_get_mixer_control (self->audio_manager);
   if (mixer_control)
     g_return_if_fail (mixer_control);
